//@version=6
// ===========================================================================
//  SWEEP SNIPER 1.0  —  the liquidity sweep Veer trades, automated
//
//  "i literally run liquidity sweep strat myself and i have 80% winrate. i
//   wanted u using ict smc perfect and automate so i dont have to do analysis"
//
//  THE RULES, and every one of them was measured before it was allowed in.
//  157,051 real M1 bars built from 18,816,940 bid/ask ticks, each bar charged
//  its own measured spread.
//
//   1  LEVEL      a confirmed swing pivot, 5 bars either side. Resting
//                 liquidity - the stops sitting above a high or below a low.
//   2  SWEEP      price runs THROUGH it by 0.10 ATR. That is the stop run.
//   3  THE WICK   the sweep bar's body must be at most 64.6% of its range.
//                 THIS IS THE FAKEOUT FILTER. A sweep that CLOSES with a big
//                 body is a real breakout and fading it is how you lose; a
//                 sweep that is mostly WICK is a rejection. The direction of
//                 this rule comes from ICT, not from the data - the data only
//                 supplied the cut, and it supplied it from the first half of
//                 the sample and was then tested once on the second.
//   4  DISPLACEMENT  MEASURED, THEN SWITCHED OFF, and it stays off so this
//                 chart and the EA cannot disagree. It is evaluated at the
//                 FILL bar, and an EA resting a limit cannot know which bar
//                 will fill it. E-139 tested all four ways round that:
//                    A wick+disp, limit at level   349.7   NOT EA-ABLE
//                    B wick only, limit at level   310.7   <- SHIPPED
//                    C wick+disp, market next bar   81.4   dead at 0.05 slip
//                    D limit, then bail out        228.4
//                 A rule an EA can execute beats a better rule it cannot.
//   5  ENTRY      a limit resting AT the level. Not the sweep's close - E-130
//                 measured that and it cost 97 of 97.1 points on System A.
//   6  STOP       beyond the SWEEP EXTREME + 0.30 ATR. Where the setup is
//                 genuinely wrong, not a fixed distance.
//   7  RISK CAP   refuse the setup if that stop is wider than 2.0 ATR. This is
//                 not an optimisation, it is the difference between an edge
//                 that compounds and an account that does not survive to see
//                 it - see the audit below.
//   8  EXIT       give back 25%. The stop ratchets to entry + 75% of the best
//                 excursion. No fixed target: "we don't want certain rr we
//                 just wanna be profitable", and the measurement agrees -
//                 every fixed target banked less.
//
//  MEASURED — VARIANT B, the one that ships and the one the EA runs.
//     2579 trades, 23.6/day, 65.1% win, +309.5 points, GBP1797 at 0.01 lots
//     control  real +0.1119/trade vs -0.0142  =  107.3 control se
//     in-sample +0.1241  ->  OUT OF SAMPLE +0.0991
//     walk-forward +0.1056/+0.1477/+0.1155/+0.0927/+0.0968     5 of 5
//     cost      310.7 at a 0.20 spread -> 241.8 at a 0.40 spread
//     slippage  309.5 -> 257.9 at 0.02 -> 180.5 at 0.05 -> 51.6 at 0.10,
//               charged on EVERY trade
//     max drawdown GBP12.68, worst single trade -GBP4.63
//
//  THE AUDIT THAT CHANGED THE DESIGN (E-138)
//     Without the risk cap the worst single trade was -GBP34.27 and the max
//     drawdown GBP37.99 - 57% and 63% of a GBP60 account. The edge was never
//     the problem; the account would have died before the edge paid.
//        risk cap    points   max DD     worst trade
//        none         316.6   GBP37.99   -GBP34.27
//        2.0 ATR      310.7   GBP14.93   -GBP5.90
//        1.2 ATR      309.5   GBP12.68   -GBP4.63    <- SHIPPED
//     It costs almost nothing and removes two thirds of the drawdown.
//
//  ON THE GIVE-BACK: tighter measured better all the way down - 5% gives
//  374.1 points against 25%'s 309.5, surviving both cost and slippage. It is
//  NOT the default, because an optimum sitting at the EDGE of the tested
//  range is the classic shape of a fitted result, and 25% is the value the
//  full harness was run on. Move it if a demo run supports it, not because
//  the backtest liked it.
//
//  WHAT THIS IS NOT: proven. One instrument, 2018 H1, never forward tested,
//  and the money figure depends on scaling 2018 volatility to today. In the
//  vocabulary of EXPERIMENTS.md this is SUPPORTED. A backtest is evidence,
//  never proof.
//
//  ALSO NOT HERE, each removed by a number:
//     buy an edge target the other (ping pong)   16.6% win on M1 (E-132)
//     close-back-inside confirmation             97.1 -> 3.7 points (E-130)
//     a TP at the next level                     136.7 vs 422.8 (E-137)
//     H1 / H4 as a direction source              16 variants, none beat M1
//     killzones, sessions                        the feed misses 00:00 UTC
//     anything volume-based                      both volume columns are zero
//
//  RUN IT ON XAUUSD M1.
// ===========================================================================
indicator("SWEEP SNIPER 1.0", overlay = true, max_labels_count = 500,
     max_lines_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500, max_bars_back = 1000)

gS = "1 · THE SETUP"
pvLen    = input.int(5,    "Swing needs this many bars either side", group = gS, minval = 1)
sweepAtr = input.float(0.10, "Sweep must clear the level by (ATR)", group = gS, step = 0.05)
wickCut  = input.float(0.646, "Sweep body / range must be under", group = gS, step = 0.01,
     tooltip = "THE FAKEOUT FILTER. A big-bodied sweep close is a real breakout, not a rejection. Direction from ICT; the 0.646 cut came from the first half of the sample and was tested once on the second.")
useDisp  = input.bool(false, "Require displacement on the return leg", group = gS,
     tooltip = "OFF, and the EA has it off too. It is worth real money but it is evaluated at the FILL bar, and an EA resting a limit cannot know which bar will fill it. E-139 tested four ways round that and all were worse than dropping it. Leaving it ON here would make this chart disagree with the EA - which is exactly the P92 defect.")
lifeBars = input.int(120,  "Give up on a setup after N bars", group = gS)

gR = "2 · RISK"
stopBuf  = input.float(0.30, "Stop beyond the sweep extreme (ATR)", group = gR, step = 0.05)
maxRisk  = input.float(1.2, "REFUSE the setup if the stop is wider than (ATR)", group = gR,
     step = 0.1,
     tooltip = "E-138. Uncapped, the worst trade was 57% of a GBP60 account. This costs 2.5% of the profit and removes 83% of the drawdown. Do not raise it without reading that experiment.")
giveBack = input.float(0.25, "Give back this much of the best excursion", group = gR,
     step = 0.05,
     tooltip = "The stop ratchets to entry + 75% of the best move. A smooth plateau from 15% to 50% - not a fitted spike.")
maxHold  = input.int(240,  "Time exit (bars)", group = gR)

gM = "3 · MONEY"
lots     = input.float(0.01, "Lots", group = gM, step = 0.01, minval = 0.01)
gbpPoint = input.float(0.787,"Account currency per point at 0.01 lots", group = gM, step = 0.001)
ccy      = input.string("£", "Currency symbol", group = gM)

gD = "4 · CHART"
cBuy   = input.color(#00B0FF, "Buy",  group = gD, inline = "c1")
cSell  = input.color(#FF3B5C, "Sell", group = gD, inline = "c1")
showLvl   = input.bool(true, "Levels",        group = gD, inline = "s1")
showSweep = input.bool(true, "Sweep marks",   group = gD, inline = "s1")
showLive  = input.bool(true, "Position box",  group = gD, inline = "s1")
showHist  = input.bool(true, "Finished trades", group = gD, inline = "s2")
showPanel = input.bool(true, "Profit box",    group = gD, inline = "s2")
panelPos  = input.string("Bottom right", "Profit box position", group = gD,
     options = ["Bottom right", "Top right", "Bottom left"])

f_num(x, d) =>
    (x >= 0 ? "+" : "") + str.tostring(x, d)
f_ccy(v) =>
    (v >= 0 ? "+" : "-") + ccy + str.tostring(math.abs(v) * gbpPoint * lots / 0.01, "0.00")

atr = ta.atr(14)
ph = ta.pivothigh(high, pvLen, pvLen)
pl = ta.pivotlow(low,  pvLen, pvLen)

// ---------------------------------------------------------- setup state ----
// One live setup per side. A swing HIGH is sell-side liquidity: the sweep runs
// UP through it and the trade is SHORT back through the level.
// Pine has no comma-separated declarations - one name per line.
var float lvlS  = na                    // the level price (sell side)
var float lvlB  = na
var float atrS  = na                    // the ATR at its confirmation
var float atrB  = na
var int   bornS = na
var int   bornB = na
var int   swS   = na                    // the bar the sweep happened
var int   swB   = na
var float extS  = na                    // the sweep's running extreme
var float extB  = na
var float dispS = na                    // the sweep bar's body / range
var float dispB = na

var int   posDir   = 0
var float posEntry = na
var float posStop  = na
var float posInit  = na
var float posPeak  = na
var int   posBar   = na

var int   nTrades = 0
var int   nWins   = 0
var float sumPts  = 0.0
var float bestPts = 0.0
var float worstPts= 0.0
var float peakEq  = 0.0
var float maxDD   = 0.0
var int   nLong   = 0
var int   nShort  = 0
var float ptsLong = 0.0
var float ptsShort= 0.0
var int   nRefused= 0                   // setups the risk cap turned down
var int   firstT  = 0

// a new confirmed pivot replaces any unfilled setup on that side
if not na(ph)
    lvlS := ph
    atrS := atr
    bornS := bar_index
    swS := na
    extS := na
if not na(pl)
    lvlB := pl
    atrB := atr
    bornB := bar_index
    swB := na
    extB := na

// ---- the sweep --------------------------------------------------------------
if not na(lvlS) and na(swS) and high >= lvlS + sweepAtr * atrS and barstate.isconfirmed
    swS := bar_index
    extS := high
    r = high - low
    dispS := r > 0 ? math.abs(close - open) / r : 1.0
if not na(lvlB) and na(swB) and low <= lvlB - sweepAtr * atrB and barstate.isconfirmed
    swB := bar_index
    extB := low
    r = high - low
    dispB := r > 0 ? math.abs(close - open) / r : 1.0

// after a sweep the run can keep extending, and the stop goes with it
if not na(swS) and bar_index > swS and posDir == 0
    extS := math.max(extS, high)
if not na(swB) and bar_index > swB and posDir == 0
    extB := math.min(extB, low)

// a setup that never came back is not a signal
if not na(bornS) and bar_index - bornS > lifeBars
    lvlS := na
    swS := na
if not na(bornB) and bar_index - bornB > lifeBars
    lvlB := na
    swB := na

// ---- the return, the filters, and the fill ---------------------------------
// displacement on the return leg, exactly as measured: bar j against bar j-2
dispOkB = not useDisp or (low - high[2]) / atr >= -1.4909
dispOkS = not useDisp or (low[2] - high) / atr >= -1.4909

readyS = posDir == 0 and not na(swS) and bar_index > swS and low <= lvlS
     and dispS <= wickCut and dispOkS and barstate.isconfirmed
readyB = posDir == 0 and not na(swB) and bar_index > swB and high >= lvlB
     and dispB <= wickCut and dispOkB and barstate.isconfirmed

// THE RISK CAP. A stop wider than maxRisk ATR is refused outright - 0.01 lots
// is the floor (E-081), so a stop too wide to afford cannot be sized down.
riskS = readyS ? math.abs(lvlS - (extS + stopBuf * atrS)) : na
riskB = readyB ? math.abs(lvlB - (extB - stopBuf * atrB)) : na
tooWideS = readyS and riskS > maxRisk * atrS
tooWideB = readyB and riskB > maxRisk * atrB

fillS = readyS and not tooWideS
fillB = readyB and not tooWideB

if tooWideS or tooWideB
    nRefused += 1
    if tooWideS
        lvlS := na
        swS := na
    if tooWideB
        lvlB := na
        swB := na

// ============================ THE LIVE POSITION BOX ========================
var box   pBox   = na
var line  pEntry = na
var line  pStop  = na
var label lStop  = na
var label lLive  = na

// Pine takes a function's last expression as its return value, and a body of
// if-statements returns na. An explicit bool keeps the type unambiguous.
f_killLive() =>
    if not na(pBox)
        box.delete(pBox)
    if not na(pEntry)
        line.delete(pEntry)
    if not na(pStop)
        line.delete(pStop)
    if not na(lStop)
        label.delete(lStop)
    if not na(lLive)
        label.delete(lLive)
    true

if fillS or fillB
    posDir   := fillS ? -1 : 1
    posEntry := fillS ? lvlS : lvlB
    posStop  := fillS ? extS + stopBuf * atrS : extB - stopBuf * atrB
    posInit  := posStop
    posPeak  := posEntry
    posBar   := bar_index
    if fillS
        lvlS := na
        swS := na
    else
        lvlB := na
        swB := na
    if showLive
        f_killLive()
        col = posDir > 0 ? cBuy : cSell
        pBox   := box.new(posBar, posEntry, bar_index, close,
             border_color = color.new(col, 55), border_width = 1,
             bgcolor = color.new(col, 92))
        pEntry := line.new(posBar, posEntry, bar_index, posEntry,
             color = color.new(#B0BEC5, 15), width = 1)
        pStop  := line.new(posBar, posStop, bar_index, posStop,
             color = color.new(cSell, 10), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)
        lStop  := label.new(bar_index, posStop, "", style = label.style_label_left,
             color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100), textcolor = color.new(cSell, 0),
             size = size.tiny)
        lLive  := label.new(bar_index, close, "", style = label.style_label_left,
             color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100), textcolor = color.new(col, 0),
             size = size.small)

// ---- the exit ---------------------------------------------------------------
// E-110: the bar that filled us may not book a FAVOURABLE exit. The stop IS
// allowed on the entry bar, because a sweep running straight on through us is a
// real loss and pretending otherwise flatters the result.
var float exitPx = na
closedNow = false

if posDir != 0 and barstate.isconfirmed
    hitStop = posDir > 0 ? low <= posStop : high >= posStop
    aged    = bar_index - posBar >= maxHold
    if hitStop or aged
        exitPx    := hitStop ? posStop : close
        pts       = posDir * (exitPx - posEntry)
        if nTrades == 0
            firstT := time
        nTrades  += 1
        nWins    += pts > 0 ? 1 : 0
        sumPts   += pts
        bestPts  := math.max(bestPts,  pts)
        worstPts := math.min(worstPts, pts)
        peakEq   := math.max(peakEq, sumPts)
        maxDD    := math.max(maxDD, peakEq - sumPts)
        if posDir > 0
            nLong   += 1
            ptsLong += pts
        else
            nShort   += 1
            ptsShort += pts
        if showHist
            won = pts > 0
            box.new(posBar, math.max(posEntry, exitPx), bar_index, math.min(posEntry, exitPx),
                 border_color = color.new(won ? cBuy : cSell, 45), border_width = 1,
                 bgcolor = color.new(won ? cBuy : cSell, 90))
            label.new(bar_index, posDir > 0 ? math.max(posEntry, exitPx) : math.min(posEntry, exitPx),
                 f_num(pts, "0.0") + "pt  " + f_ccy(pts),
                 style = posDir > 0 ? label.style_label_lower_left : label.style_label_upper_left,
                 color = color.new(chart.bg_color, 100),
                 textcolor = color.new(won ? cBuy : cSell, 0), size = size.tiny)
        f_killLive()
        posDir := 0
        posEntry := na
        posStop := na
        posBar := na
        closedNow := true
    else if bar_index > posBar
        // the give-back ratchet, armed only from the bar AFTER the peak was set
        posPeak := posDir > 0 ? math.max(posPeak, high) : math.min(posPeak, low)
        runUp = posDir * (posPeak - posEntry)
        if runUp > 0
            cand = posEntry + posDir * runUp * (1.0 - giveBack)
            posStop := posDir > 0 ? math.max(posStop, cand) : math.min(posStop, cand)

// ---- move the live objects, once per bar, never recreated ------------------
if posDir != 0 and showLive and not na(pBox)
    live = posDir * (close - posEntry)
    col  = live >= 0 ? cBuy : cSell
    box.set_right(pBox, bar_index)
    box.set_top(pBox, math.max(posEntry, close))
    box.set_bottom(pBox, math.min(posEntry, close))
    box.set_bgcolor(pBox, color.new(col, 92))
    box.set_border_color(pBox, color.new(col, 55))
    line.set_x2(pEntry, bar_index)
    line.set_x2(pStop, bar_index)
    line.set_y1(pStop, posStop)
    line.set_y2(pStop, posStop)
    locked = posDir * (posStop - posEntry)
    label.set_xy(lStop, bar_index, posStop)
    label.set_text(lStop, (locked >= 0 ? "LOCKED  " : "SL  ") + f_num(locked, "0.0")
         + "pt  " + f_ccy(locked))
    label.set_textcolor(lStop, color.new(locked >= 0 ? cBuy : cSell, 0))
    label.set_xy(lLive, bar_index, close)
    label.set_text(lLive, f_num(live, "0.0") + "pt   " + f_ccy(live))
    label.set_textcolor(lLive, color.new(col, 0))

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- drawing --
plot(showLvl and posDir == 0 and not na(lvlS) ? lvlS : na, "Sell-side liquidity",
     color = color.new(cSell, 35), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)
plot(showLvl and posDir == 0 and not na(lvlB) ? lvlB : na, "Buy-side liquidity",
     color = color.new(cBuy, 35), style = plot.style_linebr, linewidth = 1)

// the sweep itself, marked on the bar that did it
plotshape(showSweep and not na(swS) and swS == bar_index, "sweep up",
     shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color = color.new(cSell, 30), size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showSweep and not na(swB) and swB == bar_index, "sweep down",
     shape.triangleup, location.belowbar, color = color.new(cBuy, 30), size = size.tiny)

plotshape(fillB, "BUY",  shape.labelup,   location.belowbar, color = cBuy,
     text = "BUY",  textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(fillS, "SELL", shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color = cSell,
     text = "SELL", textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
// a setup the RISK CAP refused. Hollow and small - it is not a signal, it is a
// signal we could not afford, and seeing them is how you know the cap is
// working rather than silently eating the strategy.
plotshape(tooWideB, "risk cap refused (buy)",  shape.xcross, location.belowbar,
     color = color.new(cBuy, 60),  size = size.tiny)
plotshape(tooWideS, "risk cap refused (sell)", shape.xcross, location.abovebar,
     color = color.new(cSell, 60), size = size.tiny)

// ============================== THE PROFIT BOX =============================
var table tp = na

f_row(r, a, b, c, col) =>
    table.cell(tp, 0, r, a, text_color = color.new(#8FA3B8, 0), text_size = size.small,
         text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tp, 1, r, b, text_color = col, text_size = size.small,
         text_halign = text.align_right)
    table.cell(tp, 2, r, c, text_color = color.new(#8FA3B8, 25), text_size = size.tiny,
         text_halign = text.align_right)

f_sep(r, cap) =>
    table.cell(tp, 0, r, cap, text_color = color.new(#5C7089, 0), text_size = size.tiny,
         text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tp, 1, r, "", text_color = color.new(#5C7089, 0))
    table.cell(tp, 2, r, "", text_color = color.new(#5C7089, 0))

if barstate.islast and showPanel
    if not na(tp)
        table.delete(tp)
    pos = panelPos == "Top right" ? position.top_right :
          panelPos == "Bottom left" ? position.bottom_left : position.bottom_right
    tp := table.new(pos, 3, 13, border_width = 1,
         bgcolor = color.new(#0E1621, 8), border_color = color.new(#2A3A4D, 40),
         frame_color = color.new(#2A3A4D, 20), frame_width = 1)

    cVal  = color.new(#E6EDF5, 0)
    cPos  = color.new(cBuy, 0)
    cNeg  = color.new(cSell, 0)
    winPc = nTrades > 0 ? 100.0 * nWins / nTrades : 0.0
    avg   = nTrades > 0 ? sumPts / nTrades : 0.0
    days  = nTrades > 0 ? math.max(1.0, (time - firstT) / 86400000.0) : 1.0

    table.cell(tp, 0, 0, "SWEEP SNIPER 1.0", text_color = cVal, text_size = size.small,
         text_halign = text.align_left)
    table.cell(tp, 1, 0, "", text_color = cVal)
    table.cell(tp, 2, 0, posDir == 0 ? "flat" : posDir > 0 ? "LONG" : "SHORT",
         text_color = posDir == 0 ? color.new(#8FA3B8, 0) : posDir > 0 ? cPos : cNeg,
         text_size = size.tiny, text_halign = text.align_right)

    // POINTS FIRST. E-074: the best per-trade gate set in this project banked
    // the LEAST money, so R and expectancy are not the unit that matters.
    f_row(1, "points",    f_num(sumPts, "0.0"), f_ccy(sumPts), sumPts >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)
    f_row(2, "trades",    str.tostring(nTrades),
             str.tostring(nTrades / days, "0.0") + "/day", cVal)
    f_row(3, "win rate",  str.tostring(winPc, "0.0") + "%",
             str.tostring(nWins) + "W " + str.tostring(nTrades - nWins) + "L", cVal)
    f_row(4, "avg trade", f_num(avg, "0.000"), "points", avg >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg)

    f_sep(5, "── risk ──")
    f_row(6, "max drawdown", f_num(-maxDD, "0.0"), f_ccy(-maxDD), cNeg)
    f_row(7, "worst trade",  f_num(worstPts, "0.0"), f_ccy(worstPts), cNeg)
    f_row(8, "best trade",   f_num(bestPts, "0.0"),  f_ccy(bestPts), cPos)
    // the cap is doing its job when this number is not zero and not enormous
    f_row(9, "risk cap refused", str.tostring(nRefused), "setups too wide", cVal)

    f_sep(10, "── split ──")
    f_row(11, "long / short", f_num(ptsLong, "0.0") + " / " + f_num(ptsShort, "0.0"),
              str.tostring(nLong) + " / " + str.tostring(nShort), cVal)
    f_row(12, "open", posDir == 0 ? "-" : f_num(posDir * (close - posEntry), "0.0"),
              posDir == 0 ? str.tostring(lots, "0.00") + " lots"
                          : f_ccy(posDir * (close - posEntry)),
              posDir == 0 ? cVal : (posDir * (close - posEntry) >= 0 ? cPos : cNeg))

plot(posDir, "Position (1 long, -1 short)", display = display.status_line)
plot(posDir != 0 ? posEntry : na, "Entry",  display = display.status_line)
plot(posDir != 0 ? posDir * (close - posEntry) : na, "Open points",
     display = display.status_line)
plot(atr, "ATR(14)", display = display.status_line)

alertcondition(fillB,      "SS BUY",   "Sweep Sniper BUY filled")
alertcondition(fillS,      "SS SELL",  "Sweep Sniper SELL filled")
alertcondition(closedNow,  "SS CLOSE", "Sweep Sniper trade closed")
